target.body:
Closes #105940

## What Problem This Solves

`openclaw doctor --fix` could drop an inherited Google Chat `accounts.default.blockStreaming` setting when migrating a named account that only had a flat streaming key such as `chunkMode`. Runtime then treated the named account's partial `streaming` object as a wholesale replacement, so block streaming silently turned off for that account.

## Why This Change Was Made

Google Chat named-account resolution layers `accounts.default` before the named account and replaces `streaming` wholesale (same inheritance shape as WhatsApp). The generic root-only seeding path (`accountStreamingReplacesRoot`) only copied channel-root streaming into newly materialized account objects and never consulted `accounts.default`.

This mirrors the WhatsApp plugin-local `seedMigratedAccountStreaming` repair from #105709: migrate flat aliases, then deep-fill missing fields from `accounts.default` (falling back to root) for accounts that did not already have a nested `streaming` object.

## User Impact

Multi-account Google Chat configs that shared block-streaming (or other delivery settings) via `accounts.default` keep those settings after `openclaw doctor --fix`, instead of losing them when a named account also had a flat streaming key to migrate.

## Evidence

# OpenClaw PR #106018 real behavior proof
# Date: 2026-07-13T07:00:24Z
# Head under test: e87445a25ba46babf68118fff1e786c3cbf1d7c9 (PR doctor-contract in dist)
# Fixture: isolated OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH / OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR / HOME (no credentials)

## 1) Before doctor
{
  "enabled": true,
  "accounts": {
    "default": {
      "blockStreaming": true
    },
    "support": {
      "chunkMode": "newline"
    }
  }
}

## 2) openclaw doctor --fix --non-interactive --yes (migration panel)
│
◇  Legacy config keys detected ────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                          │
│  - channels.googlechat.accounts:                                         │
│    channels.googlechat.accounts.<id>.chunkMode, blockStreaming, and      │
│    blockStreamingCoalesce are legacy; use                                │
│    channels.googlechat.accounts.<id>.streaming.{chunkMode,block.enabled  │
│    ,block.coalesce}.                                                     │
│    Run "openclaw doctor --fix".                                          │
│                                                                          │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
│
◇  Doctor changes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                    │
│  Moved channels.googlechat.accounts.default.blockStreaming →       │
│  channels.googlechat.accounts.default.streaming.block.enabled.     │
│  Moved channels.googlechat.accounts.support.chunkMode →            │
│  channels.googlechat.accounts.support.streaming.chunkMode.         │
│  Copied effective channels.googlechat streaming defaults into      │
│  channels.googlechat.accounts.support.streaming to keep inherited  │
│  settings while migrating flat streaming keys.                     │
│                                                                    │
├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯

## 3) Persist via doctor write path (replaceConfigFile / allowConfigSizeDrop)
wrote /tmp/openclaw-106018-evidence-fWqD/openclaw.json

## 4) After-fix channels.googlechat
{
  "enabled": true,
  "accounts": {
    "default": {
      "streaming": {
        "block": {
          "enabled": true
        }
      },
      "groupPolicy": "allowlist"
    },
    "support": {
      "streaming": {
        "chunkMode": "newline",
        "block": {
          "enabled": true
        }
      },
      "groupPolicy": "allowlist"
    }
  },
  "groupPolicy": "allowlist"
}

## 5) Resolved named-account streaming (post-migration accounts.support.streaming; runtime replaces default wholesale)
{
  "chunkMode": "newline",
  "block": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}

## Proof assertion
PASS: retained accounts.default block.enabled + named chunkMode

## Notes
- Crabbox binary unavailable in this environment; used local isolated fixture with OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH/STATE_DIR/HOME.
- Full CLI doctor prints the migration panel (including layered accounts.default seeding) then hits an existing InvalidConfigError while later health steps still see the pre-write on-disk flat keys; the doctor migrate+replaceConfigFile write path used above is the same persistence API doctor write-config uses and persists the rewrite successfully.
- No credentials or account identifiers were used.
